Subject: [P20 review] winedmo retain codec admission and format validation

Residual against GE-Proton11-9 after ge-video-rework.
Source-reviewed only: not compiler or runtime qualification.
Prior P19b2 patch ownership (some behavior is now upstream):
  ge-master-20260913-se2-p10/0050-winedmo-expose-existing-mjpeg-video-decoder.patch
  ge-master-20260913-se2-p12/0051-winedmo-expose-existing-mpeg-video-decoders.patch
  ge-master-20260913-se2-p12/0052-winedmo-register-existing-mpeg4-video-aliases.patch
  ge-master-20260913-se2-p8/0047-winedmo-expose-ac3-and-eac3-audio-decoding.patch
  proposed/0027-winedmo-expose-vp8-and-hevc-decoders.patch
  proposed/0033-winedmo-bound-and-extend-audio-channel-counts.patch
  proposed/0042-winedmo-expose-existing-flac-audio-decoder.patch
  proposed/0048-winedmo-expose-existing-dts-alac-and-g711-decoders.patch
